'''Gluttony''' is a [[mini-boss]] and one of the [[Seven Deadly Sins]].

== Behavior ==
Gluttony wanders randomly around the room and performs one of two attacks:
* Shoots 8 projectiles in all directions.
* Fires a {{i|Brimstone}} laser from his belly towards Isaac if he is aligned in a cardinal direction.
Gluttony deals a whole heart of contact damage.

== Notes ==
* {{dlc|anr}} Occasionally, 2 regular Gluttonies appear in a Mini-Boss Room and the boss message will display "Isaac vs {{E|Super Gluttony}}".
* {{dlc|nr}} Gluttony can drop {{i|<3}} even if Isaac has already encountered/possessed it. 
== Unlockable [[Achievement]]s ==
{{achievement text | The Book of Sin }}

== Trivia ==
* Gluttony is essentially a {{E|Vis}} with an attached head. The same applies to {{E|Super Gluttony}}, except his body is that of a {{E|Double Vis}}.
* The [[wikipedia:Seven Deadly Sins|Seven Deadly Sins]] that these mini-bosses are based upon are, in Christian teachings, a classification of vices from which all others are derived from.
* Gluttony is a personification of one of the Seven Deadly Sins. Gluttony is the distorted desire to experience pleasures related to eating and drinking. It is a type of hedonism that could involve things such as over-eating, excessively unhealthy eating, alcohol abuse, and spending excessive amounts of money of luxurious foods, among other things. Gluttony is believed to open up a person to impulsivity, dullness in religious thought, as well as other kinds of hedonism such as lust.

